      "id": "2081624723432124681",
      "text": "I don’t pay the protection money to the media",
      "created_at": "Mon Jul 27 06:16:23 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": null,
      "quoted": {
        "id": "2081398673439641990",
        "text": "I sat on the syndicate desk of a global investment bank from the dot-com crash through the global financial crisis.\n\nWe had to do a lot of media work to promote deals. One day I asked our Global Head of Communications why the media was so gentle with us.\n\nHe laughed:\n“Because we’re one of their biggest advertisers.”\n\nThat explains a lot of the media’s treatment of Elon.\n\nTesla is so successful, its ad spend is effectively zero, or ~0.01% of the $40 billion global auto advertising market.\n\nNo ad dollars = no protection.\n\nNo one knows this better than Big Pharma.\n\nThey don't make confusing and enigmatic ads to sell you product; they make the ads to control the media.",
